AWS IAM – Quick Tips & Key Points

🔐 IAM (Identity & Access Management) is the backbone of AWS security. Always follow best practices:

✅ Never use Root User for daily tasks – create IAM users instead  
✅ Enable MFA (Multi-Factor Authentication) for extra security  
✅ Follow Principle of Least Privilege – give only required permissions  
✅ Use IAM Roles instead of access keys for services (EC2, Lambda, etc.)  
✅ Avoid hardcoding Access Keys in code – use roles or secure services like Secrets Manager  
✅ Regularly rotate credentials and remove unused users/keys  
✅ Use Groups to manage permissions efficiently  
✅ Enable CloudTrail for auditing and tracking activities  
✅ Use IAM Policies carefully – prefer managed policies over inline where possible  

💡 Pro Tip:  
👉 “If your architecture depends on access keys, rethink it. Use IAM Roles wherever possible.”

🔒 Secure IAM = Secure AWS Account
